WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.692
In January 1936, in a New Jersey courthouse, the most

2
00:00:03.692 --> 00:00:06.700
famous scientist in the world put his name to a

3
00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:10.668
government form declaring that he meant to become an American.

4
00:00:11.018 --> 00:00:14.288
Einstein was born in Ulm, in the kingdom of

5
00:00:14.288 --> 00:00:17.635
Württemberg, in 1879, and grew up in Munich.

6
00:00:17.985 --> 00:00:21.483
In 1905, working as a clerk in the Swiss patent office

7
00:00:21.483 --> 00:00:24.917
in Bern, he published the papers that remade physics.

8
00:00:25.266 --> 00:00:28.760
Einstein held professorships in Zurich, Prague and

9
00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:33.092
Berlin, and in 1921 he was awarded the Nobel Prize in Physics.

10
00:00:33.442 --> 00:00:36.608
Einstein was abroad — lecturing in the United

11
00:00:36.608 --> 00:00:40.477
States — when Hitler became chancellor in January 1933.

12
00:00:40.827 --> 00:00:44.166
He resigned from the Prussian Academy of Sciences, gave

13
00:00:44.166 --> 00:00:47.445
up his German citizenship, and resolved not to return.

14
00:00:47.795 --> 00:00:50.149
In a public statement that March he set the

15
00:00:50.149 --> 00:00:52.613
condition under which he would live anywhere:

16
00:00:53.213 --> 00:00:57.425
“As long as I have any choice, I will only stay in a country where political

17
00:00:57.425 --> 00:01:01.804
liberty, toleration, and equality of all citizens before the law are the rule.”

18
00:01:02.404 --> 00:01:04.737
The Institute for Advanced Study, a new

19
00:01:04.737 --> 00:01:07.908
research centre in Princeton, had offered him a post.

20
00:01:08.258 --> 00:01:11.566
On 15 January 1936, Einstein filed his Declaration

21
00:01:11.566 --> 00:01:14.940
of Intention — an immigrant's sworn "first papers,"

22
00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:18.579
the formal statement that he meant to become a citizen.

23
00:01:18.929 --> 00:01:22.530
He took the oath of citizenship in 1940, keeping the

24
00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:26.339
Swiss citizenship he had held since young adulthood, so

25
00:01:26.339 --> 00:01:30.771
that he ended his life a citizen of two republics and no empire.

26
00:01:31.121 --> 00:01:34.465
He used his fame as an American deliberately: for refugees

27
00:01:34.465 --> 00:01:37.751
fleeing the same Europe he had escaped, for civil rights,

28
00:01:37.751 --> 00:01:41.152
and against the misuse of the physics he had helped create.

29
00:01:41.502 --> 00:01:45.124
If you had to choose a country to live in, what would it need to promise you?
